

                   ADVENTURER-KINGS:  GAME 3, TURN 6

                                  FOR

                   SHAMAN UGA-BUGA MAKUMBU



                              




  Quote of the Week:

  John II, King of Poland, after routing the Turks from Vienna in 1683 A.D.:
  "The immortal God... has blest us with so signal a victory as scarce the 
memory of man can equal.  Thanks be to Heaven, now the Half-Moon triumphs no 
longer over the Cross!"


ACTION REPORT    

Here's what happened to Your Majesty this turn:


  In spring, Pascal was magically charmed by Uga-Buga Makumb.  
Uga-Buga Makumb bit his fangs into Pascal and sucked up his blood.  Pascal 
changed to Pagan alignment!  Uga-Buga Makumb's efforts raised his skill in 
Necromancy.
  Congratulations!  Your kingdom has attained level 6 in Necromancy.  Your 
characters of this exalted level are awarded a new Advanced Ability: 
  NECROMANCY- PLACES OF POWER:  The Necromancer is now able to use the magic 
of certain Dark Places of Power to increase the success chance of spells.  
At any Tomb, Crypt or Catacombs, the success chance to cast a Necromancy 
spell is increased by 20%.  For Search actions, the 20% bonus is applied 
when that type of feature is searched.  For Action spells, the bonus is 
applied if that feature type is in the same province as the character, and 
is not occupied by a monster.

  Tebessa was hit by a plague.  The plague struck the 96th Bowmen and the 
269th Bowmen in Tebessa and destroyed them.
  During early summer, Constantine was magically charmed by Uga-Buga Makumb. 
Uga-Buga Makumb sank his fangs into Constantine and sucked up his blood.  
Constantine changed to Undead alignment!
  With the coming of the late summer season Uga-Buga Makumb cast a Plague 
spell.  Chaco was hit by a plague.  The Plague affected no armies in Chaco.
  Kabompo was hit by a plague.  The Plague affected no armies in Kabompo.
  With the coming of the fall season, Uga-Buga Makumb flew into Jerbilia.

  A conquering horde owing their allegiance to 
Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll invaded the province of Jerbilia, a 
Desert area owned by Kwoth (#3).  Jerbilia was conquered and occupied by 
Uga-Buga Makumb's host.  Jerbilia was discovered to have an income of 3 
gold.
  The fall season darkened into early winter.  Uga-Buga Makumb flew into 
Chaco.  Viewing the western horizon, one can see a Jungle province called 
Katanga (#404).  It is said that Circe reigns there.  It is known to be 
occupied by Dwarves.  Their Dwarven fighters fight in the style of Legion 
and Elephants.  Uga-Buga Makumb found a Tomb (#73) in Chaco, occupied by 
the Lich.  Legend says the Large Hoard of Gold is hidden here.  From wise 
soothsayers it can be learned that the Lich is a very powerful undead 
monster: an Arch-Mage of great sorcerous power who has passed into an 
unliving state of existence through force of will and powerful magic.


  A host of warriors carried the banner of 
Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll into the Plain province of Chaco, ruled 
by Kwoth.  Uga-Buga Makumb commanded the attacking armies.  The defenders 
were led by Hokuto (#4).  The armies were drawn up into lines of battle as 
shown here:

