  DEFENDING ARMY

  The attackers had the 241st Bowmen, the 110th Bowmen, the 109th 
Heavy Cavalry, the 277th Eagles and the 209th Warg Riders in reserve.  I led 
my armies into the fray.  Alaric stood ready at the head of his thousands.
  The Skeletal Armies led by Uga-Buga Makumb marched into battle with a 
fanatical fervor.  Guerin's soldiers, ill-supplied for the desert campaign, 
suffered from thirst.  Alaric's soldiers, ill-supplied in the desert, 
suffered from thirst.  I was unlucky, for I couldn't find a protected 
encampment to rest my troops the previous day, thus my men were in dismal 
condition.  On the other hand my wise tactical planning assured my side a 
clear advantage.

  Across the entire front, the Crack 108th Skeletal Bowmen faced the 130th 
Axemen.  The 124th Skeletal Dragons swooped down on the 130th Axemen and 
attacked them.  The 240th Bowmen and the 241st Bowmen flanked the enemy 
lines and charged in with full strength.  The 108th Skeletal Bowmen fought 
the 130th Axemen and cut them down like weeds.
  Having found a vulnerable spot in the line of the host of Alaric, a final 
savage slashing attack defeated their enemy and won the day for me.  The 
108th Skeletal Bowmen scattered the 130th Axemen in all directions.
  Guerin's well-planned campaign accomplished the conquest of Bir Nzaran.
  With the coming of the late summer season, Guerin's attempted cast of the 
Kill Enemy spell didn't work.  Alaric went berserk over the Kill-Enemy 
attempt.  Guided by eerily accurate psychotic visions, Alaric scouted around 
for me in Bir Nzaran.  Alaric could not encounter me because I led an army 
and Alaric didn't.
  The summer mellowed into the fall.  I could not cast Resurrection on 
Alaric because Alaric was still alive.  So, I really tried hard to improve 
my Tactics, but I practiced in vain.
  The fall darkened into a frigid early winter.  I attempted an illegal 
move.  I tried to move from Bir Nzaran to Peachwood, but provincial flooding 
and insufficient transport thwarted the move.  Instead, I practiced my 
Tactics diligently for many weeks, but could make no headway.

  Thy humble servant,   Guerin


From: Gunga Din, Squire to Teleko
To: Uga-Buga Makumb

  Honored Sovereign, 

  With the coming of the spring season Teleko set out to quench his thirst 
for adventure.  He cast a Plague spell.  Limerick was hit by a plague.  The 
Plague affected no armies in Limerick.
  During early summer, Teleko cast a Kill Enemy spell and Clarambald was 
magically killed by a dark Necromantic spell!  And so it was that Clarambald 
met his unseemly end.  His efforts raised his aptitude in Necromancy.
  In late summer, Clarambald was resurrected by the spell cast by Teleko.
  With the coming of the fall season, Teleko flew over to Gafsa.  Looking to 
the northeast, one can see a Sea area, which is known as the Barents Sea 
(#802).  It is populated by no races and Kwoth rules there.

  A great host of warriors carried the banner of 
Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll into the Desert province of Gafsa, ruled 
by Kwoth (#3).  Gafsa was overrun by Teleko's host.  Gafsa was discovered to 
have a tax base of 2 gold.
  In early winter, Teleko rode his flying armies into Limerick.

  Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll ordered an invasion force into the 
adjacent Plain province of Limerick, owned by Kwoth.  Teleko was in command 
of the invading armies.  The defenders were led by Kwoth.  The armies were 
drawn up into lines of battle as shown here:

