  Teleko led his armies boldly into the battle.  Kwoth stood determinedly at 
the head of his thousands.  Circe (#8) led a host of loyal soldiers into the 
battle.
  Teleko strode forward and challenged Kwoth (#3) to personal combat.  Kwoth 
answered the challenge to honorable combat.  Lifting his hands high in the 
air, Teleko cast a Spiritwrack spell, to make Kwoth quake and shiver with 
spiritual convulsions.
  Kwoth advanced to bow range.  Waving his hands, Teleko orchestrated 
supernatural forces of magic, casting a Holy Symbol spell.  A golden mist in 
the shape of a cross formed around Teleko.
  Kwoth charged into the melee.  Showing no fear, Kwoth moved closer and 
swang at Teleko and inflicted 3 damage points on him.  His spell was 
disrupted by the event.
  Kwoth swang at Teleko but his aim was slightly off the mark.  Teleko 
violently attacked Kwoth but Kwoth evaded the blow.  Kwoth deftly swang at 
Teleko and would have hit him if Teleko hadn't ducked just then.  Teleko 
forced back Kwoth with his spirited assault.  He then thrust at Kwoth with 
terrific strength but his sword whiffed harmlessly through the air.
  Teleko swang at Kwoth and missed badly.  Kwoth maneuvered for a good 
attacking vantage.  Then Kwoth swang at Teleko with all his might but his 
aim was just off the mark.  He thrust at his nemesis but Teleko dodged the 
sword.  Hoping to take advantage of a gap in Kwoth's defenses, Teleko thrust 
at Kwoth and scored on him, doing 2 points of damage.  Kwoth daringly swang 
at Teleko and would have hit him if Teleko hadn't ducked just then.  With 
surprising speed, Teleko thrust at Kwoth and damaged him, inflicting 5 
damage points.
  Teleko swang at Kwoth and scorched him with 2 damage points.  Kwoth 
feigned retreat, then whirled and thrust at Teleko and inflicted 3 damage 
points.  Teleko violently assailed Kwoth and inflicted 5 damage points on 
him.  Kwoth staggered, stunned by the force of the mortal blow.  Thus did 
Kwoth finally die, a defiant death by any standard.
  The forces commanded by Kwoth were disheartened by his death, yet still 
they moved ahead with some hope of victory.  Circe (#8) assumed command of 
the forces of the realm of Circe.  An unfavorable omen manifested itself, 
which of course dealt a severe blow to Teleko's hopes.  Teleko's mount was 
shot and killed while Teleko was giving a speech.  On the other hand in this 
perilous slugging match, Teleko appeared to have the tactical edge.
  The Dragons commanded by Teleko were not impressed by his lack of 
leadership ability.  Kwoth (#3) gave a rousing harangue to his troops, which 
bolstered their courage.  Circe (#8) started with a rousing harangue to her 
army, which bolstered their courage.  The Werefolk led by Circe were 
disgusted with her lack of leadership ability.
  On the left wing, the 319th Eagles faced the 261st Phalanx.  The 319th 
Eagles swooped down on the 261st Phalanx and attacked without mercy.  On 
this field, scouts of the 319th Eagles had been trapped before the battle.  
They were killed and their bodies catapulted over the 319th Eagles.  This 
goaded the 319th Eagles into a berserk attacking rage.
  But the battle was not yet over.  The 261st Phalanx's opponents were 
overjoyed when a beautiful golden eagle flew overhead, a wonderful omen.  
But their joy turned to despair when a boorish soldier killed the bird (a 
SURE sign of doom!)  The 319th Eagles fought the 261st Phalanx and battled 
them tooth and nail, neither side willing to give ground.
  Within the interior lines, the 322nd Eagles faced the 15th Phalanx.  The 
322nd Eagles swooped down on the 15th Phalanx and attacked without mercy.  
In this match, the men of the 322nd Eagles ran into some unpredictable 
footing and were afflicted with great disruption.  The 322nd Eagles fought 
the 15th Phalanx and could not hold their ground against their savage foe.
  In the interior lines, the Veteran 323rd Trolls were arrayed against the 
Crack 234th Legion.  In this area, many men of the 323rd Trolls were 
suffering from hangovers, weakening their fighting strength significantly.  
The 323rd Trolls battled the 234th Legion and could not quite hold their 
ground against their savage opponent.
  Within the interior lines, the 326th Dragons faced the 235th Legion.  The 
326th Dragons fought with the 235th Legion and could not stand their ground 
and executed an orderly retreat.
  Within the interior front, the 321st Eagles were arrayed against the 
Veteran 67th Legion.  The 321st Eagles swooped down on the 67th Legion and 
attacked them.  Here, some of the 67th Legion had been drawn off by the need 
to take a small but centrally situated castle, so they were far below their 
usual strength.  Still, the 321st Eagles battled with the 67th Legion and 
could not quite hold their ground against their determined foe.
  On the right wing, the 320th Eagles faced the 26th Were-Beasts, who were 
stiffened by a tough outfit of freedom fighters of the Mercenaries Guild, 
who led them into a fanatical fervor by example of their fearless elan.  The 
320th Eagles swooped down on the 26th Were-Beasts and attacked without 
mercy.  Here, the musicians of the 26th Were-Beasts bravely volunteered to 
march in the van, and all the soldiers were stirred by their spirited 
singing.  The 320th Eagles battled the 26th Were-Beasts and battled them to 
a standstill.
  Circe's great horde overwhelmed the army of Uga-Buga Makumb and took the 
field, scattering their enemies.
  Though Circe's forces were triumphant, Teleko rallied his men and decided 
to contest Limerick.  The battle affected the quality of our forces:  we can 
now raise the rating of the 319th Eagles to Veteran, its men having 
displayed admirable courage.  The 326th Dragons took a severe beating and 
lost some key people.  It should be rated a Green unit now.  The 321st 
Eagles was unfortunate enough to lose some of its most able officers, and we 
now rate it a Green unit.  The 320th Eagles proved its valor in the fight 
and we now rate it a Veteran unit.

  Thy humble servant,   Gunga Din, Squire to Teleko


From: Roderoch
To: Uga-Buga Makumb

  Honored Sovereign, 

  In spring, I was told by some peasants of a perilous feature in Ngara 
previously unknown to us, a Pyramid (#3) where dwells the Vampire.  Legend 
says the Large Hoard of Gold is hidden here.  From ancient tomes, it is 
known that the Vampire is an undead monster with great strength.  It loves 
to charm a human victim with its hypnotic eyes, then sink its fangs into the 
jugular vein and suck the victim dry.  I girded my weapon and entered the 
Pyramid cautiously.  I wielded my Sword Excalibur.  I encountered 
the Vampire.  I incanted my strange words of magic and cast a Holy Symbol 
spell.  A golden mist in the shape of a cross formed around me.  The spell 
caused the Vampire to moan in excruciating agony and damaged the Vampire, 
scoring 8 damage points.  The Vampire's spell was disrupted by the event.  
Chanting my artful words of magic into a mighty Fireball spell, I waved my 
hands and inflicted 4 damage points.
  The Vampire moved to bow range.  I boldly shot an arrow at the Vampire and 
scored on the Vampire, doing 5 points of damage.  With unwavering strength, 
I readied an arrow and shot it at the Vampire and walloped the Vampire with 2
damage points.
  The Vampire rushed into melee combat.  The Vampire flamboyantly vaulted 
over me and punched at me but I dodged the blow.  I then swang at 
the Vampire with terrific force and missed.  The Vampire viciously swung at 
me and scored 4 damage points on me.  I thrust at the Vampire and damaged 
the Vampire, inflicting 5 damage points.
  I summoned all my will and desperately thrust at my nemesis and inflicted 6
damage points.  The Vampire dropped to the ground, mortally pierced.  I 
turned my attention to the treasure of the Vampire.  I bagged the Large 
Hoard of Gold.  I found a treasure of 14 gold and bagged it.
  I saw nothing special while scouting out the Pyramid.  In my travels, I 
encountered no marauding monsters.
  In early summer, I moved into Tebessa.  During my travels, I wielded my 
Sword Excalibur.  I was stopped by a local patrol.  Their commanding captain 
suspiciously challenged me.  But I wasn't listed as an outlaw, and that got 
me off the hook.

  Midsummer's day came and went and late summer arrived.  I also discovered 
a Dungeon (#69) in Tebessa, occupied by the Chimera.  Legend says the Book 
of Druidic Incantations is hidden here.  The Chimera is a powerful but 
unintelligent winged monster with the body of a lion and three heads, of 
lion, dragon and goat.  I girded my weapon and entered the Dungeon 
cautiously.  I drew out my Sword Excalibur.  I encountered the Chimera.  
Lifting my hands high in the air, I cast a Spiritwrack spell, to make 
the Chimera quake and shiver with spiritual convulsions.
  The Chimera moved to bow range.  I incanted my strange words of magic and 
cast a Holy Symbol spell.  A golden mist in the shape of a cross formed 
around me.  My efforts raised my skill in White Magic.
  Congratulations!  You have attained skill level 5 in White Magic.  At 
levels 5 and up, the usual 15% per level increase in the cast chance is 
discontinued, and the number of spells you can cast in White Magic is capped 
at 3 Action, 2 Combat.  The effects of the "Holy Symbol" and "Spiritwrack" 
spells are also capped at level 4 (however, skill level will still determine 
who attacks first in personal combat).  Instead, all characters of this high 
level gain the following Advanced Ability: 
  WHITE MAGIC- ENHANCED HOLY SYMBOL:  The Holy Symbol spell now has the same 
effect against opponents who have an Evil alignment as it does against 
Undead creatures.

  The Chimera rushed into melee combat.  With amazing speed, the Chimera 
energetically lunged at me and scored on me, inflicting 5 points of damage.  
My spell was disrupted by the event.  The Chimera whirled around and snapped 
at me and scorched me with 6 damage points.  I dropped to the ground, 
mortally pierced.  And so it was that I met my unseemly end.  And so, I rose 
once again to Valhalla.
  I returned to Valhalla, having tried my best to fulfill my duties.


  Thy humble servant,   Roderoch


From: Gridley, Squire to Melantheus
To: Uga-Buga Makumb

  Honored Sovereign, 

  With the advent of the spring season, Melantheus prepared to quench his 
thirst for adventure.  He was tutored in the art of Sageness by Amalric.  
Melantheus tried to practice his Sageness, but the task seemed beyond his 
natural ability.  His experience improved his aptitude in Sageness.  He 
invented nothing in his sagely researches.
  The wet spring was followed by a sultry early summer.  Melantheus was 
tutored in the art of Sageness by Amalric.  Melantheus tried to practice his 
Sageness, but the task was beyond his natural aptitude.  His efforts 
improved his aptitude in Sageness.  He discovered nothing valuable in his 
sagely researches.
  Midsummer's day came and went and a hot late summer came.  Melantheus was 
tutored in the art of Sageness by Lallipugh.  Melantheus practiced his 
Sageness and improved noticeably.  He invented nothing in his sagely 
experiments.
  With the advent of the fall season Melantheus discovered nothing worthy of 
note in his sagely researches.
  In early winter, Melantheus tried to practice his Sageness, but the task 
seemed beyond his ability.  He discovered nothing in his sagely experiments.

  Thy humble servant,   Gridley, Squire to Melantheus


From: Tao-Li
To: Uga-Buga Makumb

  Honored Sovereign, 

  Stormy winter gave way to fragrant spring, and I prepared to carry out my 
imperial orders.  I moved into the Falkland Sea (#1305) with my Fleet.  I 
found a feature in the Falkland Sea: a Cavern (#70) inhabited by 
the Rakshasha.  What treasure may lie there is unknown.  The Rakshasha is a 
strong, evil spirit encased in flesh.  Of Hindu origin, it has great powers 
of illusion.
  In early summer, I recruited enough men in the Falkland Sea to form the 
77th Fleet, the 78th Bowmen and the 97th Garrison for the army of Tao-Li.
  Midsummer's night came and went and late summer arrived.  I tried hard to 
improve my Navigation, but I practiced in vain.
  With the coming of the fall season I moved into Oceanus Cyclopia (#1405) 
with my redoubtable Fleet.
  During early winter, I sailed into the Plesiosaurus Sea (#1406) with my 
forces.  Turning to the east, one can see a Sea area, which is known as the 
Giant Crab Sea (#1506).  It is populated by no races and 
Lord Babba Sissoko Master orango rules there.  Southeast of here is the 
Atlantis Sea (#1507), a Forest province ruled by Bouticca, where Elves 
dwell.  Their Elven fighters prefer to array themselves in the style of 
Bowmen and Fleet.

  A host of savage warriors carried the banner of 
Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll into the Forest province of the 
Plesiosaurus Sea, ruled by Kurtinaitis (#62).  I was in command of the 
invading armies.  The defenders were led by Kurtinaitis.  The armies were 
drawn up into lines of battle as shown here:

  ATTACKING ARMY, Battle of the Plesiosaurus Sea (1406):

  296th   
 Marines  
 01 
          
   78th   
  Bowmen  
 }}}01}}} 
          
 297th/A  
  Axemen  
    01    
----------
 }}}62}}} 
 162nd/A  
  Bowmen  
          
  DEFENDING ARMY

  The attackers had the 77th Fleet Marines, the 97th Garrison and the 298th 
Garrison in reserve.  I led my armies boldly into the battle.  Kurtinaitis 
commanded a host of loyal soldiers into the battle.
  No luck of great importance altered the engagement.  Tao-Li's wise 
tactical planning gave my forces an undeniable advantage.

  Across the whole front, the 297th Axemen faced the 162nd Bowmen.  The 78th 
Bowmen and the 296th Fleet Marines outflanked the undermanned enemy and 
charged in with full strength.  In this engagement, the soldiers of the 
297th Axemen had lost sleep because of the local food and became slightly 
ill.  They entered battle at a slight disadvantage.  Even so, the 297th 
Axemen battled with the 162nd Bowmen and moved ahead slowly, contested for 
every foot of their advance.
  Having found a vulnerable spot in the line of the host of Kurtinaitis, a 
final determined thrust finished off their opponent and won the day for me.  
The 78th Bowmen chased after the enemy and were beaten off by the 162nd 
Bowmen in a tough rearguard action.  The 296th Fleet Marines overtook the 
enemy and were driven off by the 162nd Bowmen in a hard-fought rearguard 
battle.
  Although Tao-Li's host were victorious, Kurtinaitis rallied his forces and 
prepared to contest the Plesiosaurus Sea.  The battle affected the quality 
of our forces:  the 78th Bowmen proved its valor during the fight and we now 
rate it an Average unit.  The 296th Fleet was greatly buoyed by the victory. 
We now rate it a Veteran unit.  The 77th Fleet was tested during the battle 
and came through with flying colors.  We can now call it an Average unit.

  Thy humble servant,   Tao-Li


From: Lallipugh
To: Uga-Buga Makumb

  Honored Sovereign, 

  In spring, I tried to practice my Sageness, but the task seemed beyond my 
natural aptitude.  I discovered nothing in my sagely researches.
  The wet spring blossomed into early summer.  I was instructed in Sageness 
by Amalric.  I tried to improve my Sageness, but the task was beyond my 
ability.  I invented nothing in my sagely researches.
  Midsummer's night passed and late summer came.  I was instructed in the 
art of Sageness by Amalric.  I practiced my Sageness and my skill in 
Sageness went up.  I invented nothing in my sagely experiments.
  With the advent of the fall season, I tried to improve my Sageness, but 
the task seemed beyond my ability.  I invented nothing in my sagely 
experiments.
  The fall darkened into early winter.  I tried to practice my Sageness, but 
the task was beyond my ability.  I invented nothing valuable in my sagely 
researches.

  Thy humble servant,   Lallipugh


From: Watson, Squire to Amalric
To: Uga-Buga Makumb

  Honored Sovereign, 

  Winter gave way to fragrant spring.  Amalric practiced for many weeks and 
his skill in Sageness increased.  He invented nothing worthy of note in his 
sagely researches.
  With the coming of the early summer season in his sagely researches, 
Amalric discovered a fabulous invention called the Analytical Psychology!  
The following benefits are conferred by the Analytical Psychology:
  Analytical Psychology is taught to all characters employed by the Kingdom. 
Any Charm spell cast by a Psychic Mage on your character will work, but it 
wears off at the end of the turn, and the charmed character will never 
Search features or risk combat.

  Midsummer's day came and went and late summer arrived.  Amalric invented 
nothing valuable in his sagely experiments.
  With the advent of the fall season Amalric discovered nothing in his 
sagely experiments.
  In early winter, Amalric discovered nothing worthy of note in his sagely 
researches.

  Thy humble servant,   Watson, Squire to Amalric


From: Odysseus
To: Uga-Buga Makumb

  Honored Sovereign, 

  Frigid winter gave way to spring.  I marched on the Jellyfish Sea (#1105) 
with my forces.
  With the coming of the early summer season I moved into Falkenheim (#1106) 
with my redoubtable army.
  In late summer, I recruited the 123rd Eagles from among the people of 
Falkenheim, to serve under me.
  The sultry days of summer mellowed into fall.  I marched my command into 
Mare Tarkium (#1107).
  With the coming of the early winter season, I recruited enough men in Mare 
Tarkium to create the 249th Dragons for the army of Odysseus.

  Thy humble servant,   Odysseus


From: Montgomery, Squire to Elmer
To: Uga-Buga Makumb

  Honored Sovereign, 

  In spring, Elmer cast a Bless spell.  Ngara was magically blessed and 
prospered.  The Bless affected no armies in Ngara.
  In early summer, Elmer cast a Bless spell.  Tabora was magically blessed 
and prospered.  The Bless affected no armies in Tabora.
  In late summer, Elmer moved into Hollabrand.  In his travels, he saw no 
marauding monsters.
  The summer mellowed into fall.  Elmer journeyed to Falkenheim.  During his 
travels, a Giant Wasp came at Elmer from out of nowhere.  He stuck his tail 
between his legs and fled from the Giant Wasp as fast as his legs could 
carry Elmer!

  With the coming of the early winter season, Elmer travelled to the Dolphin 
Sea.  While adventuring, Elmer encountered no monster.
  Speaking to some farmers, Elmer heard a rumor about a Catacombs in 
Hollabrand (#1206), inhabited by the Banshee.  Some say that the Banshee 
actually owns the Manual of Spying.

  Thy humble servant,   Montgomery, Squire to Elmer


From: Mortimer, Squire to Presto
To: Uga-Buga Makumb

  Honored Sovereign, 

  In spring, Presto was instructed in the art of Sageness by Lallipugh.  
Presto practiced well and improved his ability in Sageness.  He invented 
nothing in his sagely experiments.
  The wet spring was followed by early summer.  Presto was instructed in 
Sageness by Amalric.  Presto practiced his Sageness and improved 
substantially.  He invented nothing valuable in his sagely researches.
  With the coming of the late summer season Presto unsheathed his weapon and 
entered the Hollow Tree warily.  Presto encountered the Renegade Swordsman.  
Incanting an Invisibility spell, Presto directed glowing, interlacing 
strands of magic, fading into invisibility.  His experience improved his 
skill in Illusions.  He stole towards the Renegade Swordsman's treasure, 
wishing to steal a great treasure.  Despite his stealth, he was detected by 
the Renegade Swordsman before anything could be stolen and engaged at spell 
range.
  The Renegade Swordsman loped along steadily, conserving his energy, and 
closed to bow range.  Presto stuck his tail between his legs and fled from 
the Renegade Swordsman as fast as his legs could carry Presto!
  While scouting the Hollow Tree, Presto saw a Magic Circle which seemed to 
be of a magical nature.  During his travels this season, a Werewolf 
unexpectedly rushed at Presto like a bolt from the blue.  He fled from the 
combat.

  With the coming of the fall season, Presto rode into the Jellyfish Sea.  
During his coastal explorations this season, he encountered a Giant Octopus. 
Presto swam shamelessly and fled from the combat.

  The fall season cooled into a frigid early winter.  Presto downed a 
nervous draught from his bottle of vodka, and entered the Cave.  Presto 
encountered the Medusa.  Presto waved his arms and gestured mightily, 
meaning to cast an Invisibility spell, but it backfired and a dove popped 
out of his hat instead.  He glided stealthily into what I thought was the 
treasure room of the Medusa, hands twitching with anticipation.  Presto 
tried to sneak by the Medusa, but was seen at spell range.
  The Medusa menacingly advanced to bow range.  Presto stuck his tail 
between his legs and fled from the Medusa as fast as his legs could carry 
Presto!
  Presto saw nothing special while scouting out the Cave.  While 
adventuring, Presto encountered no wandering monster.

  Thy humble servant,   Mortimer, Squire to Presto


From: Tattoo, Squire to Magnus
To: Uga-Buga Makumb

  Honored Sovereign, 

  With the coming of the spring season Magnus prepared to quench his thirst 
for glory.  He enlisted the 205th Garrison and the 224th Garrison in Kildare 
to serve the provincial garrison commander.
  The wet spring was followed by a fragrant early summer.  Magnus moved into 
the Virgo Sea.
  In late summer, Magnus journeyed to the Dolphin Sea.
  With the coming of the fall season Magnus was instructed in the art of 
Sageness by Lallipugh.  Magnus practiced his Sageness and his skill in 
Sageness went up.  He invented nothing valuable in his sagely researches.
  The fall season darkened into a frigid early winter.  Magnus was tutored 
in Sageness by Lallipugh.  Magnus practiced for many weeks and his skill in 
Sageness increased.  He invented nothing valuable in his sagely experiments.

  Thy humble servant,   Tattoo, Squire to Magnus


From: Clarambald
To: Uga-Buga Makumb

  Honored Sovereign, 

  In spring, I travelled to Tebessa.  While adventuring, I saw no wandering 
monsters.
  With the coming of the early summer season, I was magically killed by a 
dark Necromantic spell!  And so it was that I met my unseemly end.  His 
efforts raised his aptitude in Necromancy.
  In fall, I cast a Tornado spell.  Magical tornadoes hit the defenders of 
Limerick.  Tornadoes sucked up the 20th Legion in Limerick and destroyed 
them.  Tornadoes sucked up the 21st Light Cavalry in Limerick and destroyed 
them.  Tornadoes sucked up the 22nd Legion in Limerick and destroyed them.  
Tornadoes sucked up the 65th Legion in Limerick and destroyed them.  
Tornadoes sucked up the 211th Camel Corps in Limerick and destroyed them.  
Tornadoes sucked up the 246th Camel Corps in Limerick and destroyed them.  
Tornadoes sucked up the 343rd Bowmen in Limerick and destroyed them.
  The fall season cooled into a frigid early winter.  I cast a Flood spell 
and Limerick was magically flooded.

  Thy humble servant,   Clarambald


From: Constantine
To: Uga-Buga Makumb

  Honored Sovereign, 

  Midsummer's night passed and late summer arrived.  I travelled to Jerbilia.
To the southwest lies a poor Jungle area called Zululand (#506), populated 
by Humans.  It is ruled by no one.  Their Human warriors fight as Legion and 
Fleet.  Looking to the west, one can see a prosperous Desert area, which is 
known as Trouthome (#505).  It is populated by Elves and Circe rules there.  
Their Elven fighters traditionally fight in the style of Phalanx.  I 
discovered a feature in Jerbilia: a Sacred Rock (#66) inhabited by 
the Giant Eagle.  What treasure may lie there is unknown.  The Giant Eagle 
is a strong avian with a 10-foot wingspan.  It usually avoids contact with 
humans.
  In fall, I could not recruit Garrison and Garrison in Jerbilia because the 
King does not own that province, and mercenaries weren't available.  So, I 
practiced my Necromancy well, and even consulted an astrologer, but could 
not improve my Necromancy.
  The fall cooled into a frigid early winter.  I rode into Chaco.

  Thy humble servant,   Constantine


From: Montgomery, Squire to Pascal
To: Uga-Buga Makumb

  Honored Sovereign, 

  In early summer, Pascal moved into Limerick.  Northeast of here is the 
Daedalus Sea (#702), a Plain province owned by Kwoth, where Orcs dwell.  
Their Orcish warriors traditionally fight as Phalanx and Fleet.  To the 
northwest there lies a Desert province known as Berga (#602), a land of 
Humans where Kwoth rules.  Their Human fighters prefer to array themselves 
as Camel Corps.  While adventuring, Pascal encountered no wandering monster.
  With the coming of the late summer season, Pascal explored Limerick 
carefully, leaving no stone unturned, and our exploration level there has 
risen to 100%.  Pascal saw no monster.
  The sultry days of summer mellowed into the fall.  Pascal journeyed to 
Chirfa.  Viewing the western horizon, one can see a Forest province known as 
Balmwood (#503).  It is said that Circe reigns there.  It is known to be 
occupied by Elves.  Their Elven warriors traditionally fight as Bowmen.  
Northwest of here lies the province of Silvermist (#502), ruled by Circe.  
It is known to be a Mountain province inhabited by Eagles.  If need be, they 
can call on an army of Eagles to defend their territory.  Pascal encountered 
no marauding monsters.
  In early winter, Pascal wandered far and wide about Chirfa, uncovering its 
mysteries, and raising our exploration level in Chirfa to 100%.  Pascal 
found also that Chirfa has been the site of terrible battles.  Many renowned 
soldiers have given their lives on its fields: the 64th Camel Corps (Average 
Humans).  Pascal saw no monster.

  Thy humble servant,   Montgomery, Squire to Pascal


STATE OF THE NATION:

  My lord and sovereign, greatest of Kings, I humbly beg thy leave to make
report of matters of this Kingdom that may concern thy divine majesty.


DIPLOMACY 

  My lord, the following Kings have wisely allied with thy ever-
victorious majesty:                    

  Babba Sissoko (#0), 139g taxbase, 42g in treasury is of Undead alignment.
  Agesilao (#9)


