GENERAL INTELLIGENCE REPORT


Kingdom of Babba Sissoko (#0):
  In late summer, a fleet owing their allegiance to 
Lord Babba Sissoko Master orango (#0) invaded the province of the Kilkenny 
Sea, a Sea area ruled by the provincial Merman chieftain.  Riose (#52) 
commanded the attacking fleet.  The defending forces were commanded by the 
provincial Merman chieftain.  Riose's armada ended the campaign victoriously 
and conquered the Kilkenny Sea.
  In spring, Tlazolteotl (#88) flew over to the Balearic Sea.  Tlazolteotl's 
forces encountered little opposition in the Balearic Sea and Tlazolteotl 
there established our rule.
  In early summer, Tlazolteotl flew over to the Flying Fish Sea.
  Lord Babba Sissoko Master orango (#0)'s minions initiated a campaign of 
conquest directed at the Flying Fish Sea, a Sea province owing allegiance to 
Circe (#8).  Tlazolteotl (#88)'s forces took the Flying Fish Sea without any 
major battles.

Kingdom of Kwoth (#3):
  In spring, Limerick was hit by a plague.  The Daedalus Sea was hit by a 
plague.  Gafsa was hit by a plague.  The Plague affected no armies in Gafsa.

  In early summer, Khurum was hit by a plague.
  In late summer, Chaco was hit by a plague.  The Plague affected no armies 
in Chaco.  The Barents Sea was hit by a plague.
  In fall, Kwoth (#3) conducted military exercises and the 15th Phalanx rose 
in quality.
  In early winter, Limerick was magically flooded.

Kingdom of Hokuto (#4):
  In early winter, Hokuto (#4) boldly marched his forces into Chaco (#504).  
Hokuto marched with his loyal troops, eyes set in grim determination.
  The forces commanded by Hokuto were disheartened by his death, yet still 
they moved ahead with some hope of victory.
  Out on the right outside wing, the Veteran 316th Bowmen were arrayed 
against the Veteran 282nd Legion.  The 315th Dragons swooped down on the 
267th Chariots and attacked without mercy.  The poor horses of the 267th 
Chariots were spooked by the howls of the terrible Beasts they beheld.  The 
316th Bowmen battled with the 282nd Legion and steadily advanced against 
them.
  In the interior front, the 293rd Dragons were descended upon by the Circle 
of Wraiths, who goaded them into mindless fanatical battle-lust with their 
maniacal laughter.  They faced the Crack 70th Chariots.  The 293rd Dragons 
swooped down on the 70th Chariots and attacked them.  The horses of the 70th 
Chariots were frightened by the fearsome Beasts they beheld.  The horses of 
the 284th Chariots were frightened by the Beasts they were faced with.  In 
this match, the supreme commander condescended to personally ride with the 
troops of the 293rd Dragons in the front lines, inspiring them to a 
surpassing performance.  The 293rd Dragons fought with the 70th Chariots and 
advanced at will.
  Within the interior lines, the 317th Trolls were arrayed against the 
Veteran 71st Legion.  Here, the 71st Legion carelessly stumbled into a nest 
of booby traps and lost some of their best battle-hardened troops.  The 
317th Trolls fought with the 71st Legion and determinedly plowed into their 
opponents.
  In the interior lines, the Veteran 314th Dragons faced the Veteran 283rd 
Legion.  The 314th Dragons swooped down on the 283rd Legion and attacked 
without mercy.  On this battleground, the soldiers of the 314th Dragons 
noticed the presence of an encampment of trollops behind their opponents' 
lines, so they lustily concentrated their efforts to smash through.  The 
outcome seemed bleak for the brave fighters of the 283rd Legion.
  But would victory yet be snatched from the jaws of defeat?  A fantastic 
omen heartened the 283rd Legion.  A flight of silver dragons floated over, 
and their magic mists settled upon the 283rd Legion.  In spite of the 283rd 
Legion's good fortune, the 314th Dragons battled with the 283rd Legion and 
moved ahead slowly, contested for every foot of their advance.
  Out on the left outside wing, the 318th Trolls were arrayed against the 
233rd Chariots.  In this sector, the 233rd Chariots were fearful of defeat.  
But then the 233rd Chariots's regimental high priest picked up his pike and 
joined the battle, and the 233rd Chariots rallied fiercely.  In spite of the 
233rd Chariots's good luck, the 318th Trolls battled the 233rd Chariots and 
steadily advanced against them.  The acting commander withdrew to Balmwood, 
beaten but not discouraged.

Kingdom of Kahn (#6):
  In spring, Peachwood was magically flooded.


Kingdom of Circe (#8):
  In early summer, Lord Babba Sissoko Master orango (#0)'s minions initiated 
a campaign of conquest directed at the Flying Fish Sea, a Sea province owing 
allegiance to Circe (#8).  Tlazolteotl (#88)'s forces took the Flying Fish 
Sea without any major battles.


END MOVES REPORT

  Congratulations!  You have reached skill level 5 in Necromancy.  At levels 5
and up, the usual 15% per level increase in the cast chance is discontinued, 
and the number of spells you can cast in Necromancy is capped at 3 Action, 2 
Combat.  The effects of the "Skeletal Armies", "Plague" and "Hand of Death" 
spells are also capped at level 4 (however, skill level will still determine 
who attacks first in personal combat).  Instead, all characters of this high 
level gain the following Advanced Ability: 
  NECROMANCY- "GATE DEMON" SPELL (abbreviated "GD"):  By the dark power of 
this spell, an extra-dimensional gate is opened to the nether worlds, from 
where a demon is summoned to fight in place of the spellcaster.  The caster 
has no control over what type of demon will appear.  If the Demon wins, it 
will return to the Abyss from whence it came.  If it loses, the caster must 
continue the fight at the current combat range.  If another Mirror Image or 
Gate Demon spell is cast against it, both spells will be nullified.  A Demon 
may refuse to fight an opponent of Evil to Undead alignment (50% chance).  
Note: with old Saga programs, order this spell with "GI 28".


END MOVES REPORT

  Congratulations!  Your kingdom has reached skill level 6 in Necromancy.  
Your characters of this exalted level gain a new Advanced Ability: 
  NECROMANCY- PLACES OF POWER:  The Necromancer is now able to use the magic 
of certain Dark Places of Power to increase the success chance of spells.  
At any Tomb, Crypt or Catacombs, the success chance to cast a Necromancy 
spell is increased by 20%.  For Search actions, the 20% bonus is applied 
when that type of feature is searched.  For Action spells, the bonus is 
applied if that feature type is in the same province as the character, and 
is not occupied by a monster.


END MOVES REPORT

  Congratulations!  Your kingdom has attained level 5 in White Magic.  At 
levels 5 and up, the usual 15% per level increase in the cast chance is 
discontinued, and the number of spells you can cast in White Magic is capped 
at 3 Action, 2 Combat.  The effects of the "Holy Symbol" and "Spiritwrack" 
spells are also capped at level 4 (however, skill level will still determine 
who attacks first in personal combat).  Instead, all characters of this 
exalted level gain a new Advanced Ability: 
  WHITE MAGIC- ENHANCED HOLY SYMBOL:  The Holy Symbol spell now has the same 
effect against opponents who have an Evil alignment as it does against 
Undead creatures.


END MOVES REPORT

      

